# Keep the build context to exactly what the image needs.
#
# The Dockerfile does only `COPY requirements.txt .` and `COPY main.py .`, so
# everything else here is dead weight in the context. More importantly, without
# this file `.git` (full history) and `.gitea` (CI config, internal clone URLs)
# are sent to the daemon as part of every build.
#
# Anything added to the Dockerfile's COPY set must be allowed here, or the build
# fails with a confusing "not found" rather than a clear error.

# ─── VCS / CI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitea
.github

# ─── Not needed at runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tests
*.md
LICENSE
CHANGELOG.md
SECURITY.md
requirements-dev.txt
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml

# ─── Python / editor / OS cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv
env
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store

# ─── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
